WEBVTT

00:01:35.610 --> 00:01:36.710
Good morning!

00:01:36.710 --> 00:01:37.780
Ah! Good morning!

00:01:38.310 --> 00:01:41.080
That cake yesterday was really good, wasn't it?

00:01:47.090 --> 00:01:49.930
Was there a guy like that here before?

00:01:49.930 --> 00:01:51.580
Is he a transfer student?

00:01:52.890 --> 00:01:55.580
{- Missing Translation -}{AMS: too quiet to bother with for me}{Dark: I differ}

00:01:52.890 --> 00:01:55.580
Compared to Kaido that reeks of sweat, this is totally different!

00:01:55.580 --> 00:02:00.190
<i>Damn! This guy's acting all friendly with my Kaoru-chan!</i>

00:02:00.190 --> 00:02:01.400
<i>Could it be!?</i>

00:02:01.870 --> 00:02:04.860
<i>The guy that Kaoru-chan likes is...!</i>

00:02:04.860 --> 00:02:08.170
Hey, Honda. I roughly understand your present situation,

00:02:08.170 --> 00:02:10.440
but are you serious about starting a baseball team here?

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:11.410
{Huh?}

00:02:11.410 --> 00:02:13.910
Putting aside the new students coming in next year, 

00:02:13.910 --> 00:02:16.700
there's no way that all seven of the guys here will play baseball, right?

00:02:17.460 --> 00:02:18.700
{Huh? }It'll be fine!

00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:23.050
Fuji-kun, who joined so quickly, already promised he'd do it.

00:02:23.050 --> 00:02:24.640
W-Who said that!?

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:27.060
When did I ever say that I'd play baseball!?

00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:28.780
Don't be stubborn. 

00:02:28.780 --> 00:02:31.660
Besides, you'll end up playing sooner or later anyway!

00:02:37.750 --> 00:02:39.840
Huh? A transfer student?

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:43.440
He's a baseball idiot with a big attitude. 

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:48.560
It seems like he's going to start a baseball team and get all the guys in school to play baseball.

00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:50.630
Baseball?

00:02:50.630 --> 00:02:53.230
All the guys? As in all of us?

00:02:53.230 --> 00:02:54.430
That's impossible.

00:02:54.430 --> 00:02:57.830
Why do we have to go and play baseball?

00:02:57.830 --> 00:03:01.150
Who knows? Ask the person in question directly... 

00:03:01.150 --> 00:03:05.030
since he's probably coming to this class where the guys are gathered.

00:03:07.350 --> 00:03:14.410
<i>Man, I guess school life with those useless guys is starting again, huh? </i>

00:03:14.790 --> 00:03:17.280
<i>Everyone around me are goody-goodies... </i>

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:20.290
<i>I didn't do anything exciting over summer break.</i>

00:03:20.290 --> 00:03:24.060
<i>I should have gone to a normal co-ed school after all.</i>

00:03:24.950 --> 00:03:29.360
<i>I can't stand these unglamorous days of youth anymore.</i>

00:03:30.740 --> 00:03:32.910
All right... back to your seats!

00:03:40.600 --> 00:03:44.380
Today's the start of the second semester,
but before that, let me introduce a transfer student. 

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:48.500
This is Shigeno Goro-kun.

00:03:49.560 --> 00:03:50.830
Hey there!

00:03:51.640 --> 00:03:53.520
He's pretty cute!

00:03:55.170 --> 00:03:58.810
He's in the sports program, so some of his classes are different, 

00:03:58.810 --> 00:04:00.480
but he's your 2-A classmate.

00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:02.580
Everyone, please get along with him.

00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:04.930
<i>I'm estimating that he's 180cm tall and weighs 70kg. </i>

00:04:05.420 --> 00:04:07.900
<i>A solidly built athlete...</i>

00:04:07.900 --> 00:04:10.900
He's totally my type!

00:04:13.150 --> 00:04:16.630
Hey, hey, Shigeno-kun, where did you go to school before?

00:04:16.630 --> 00:04:17.920
{missing tl}What kind of sports did you play?

00:04:17.920 --> 00:04:20.660
{missing tl2}

00:04:17.920 --> 00:04:20.860
Hey, sorry, I've got something I need to do so...

00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:22.120
{missing tl3}

00:04:21.490 --> 00:04:22.930
{Huh? }There they are!

00:04:22.930 --> 00:04:24.040
Hey!

00:04:25.150 --> 00:04:26.780
Wait up!

00:04:28.360 --> 00:04:32.510
Ignoring the lonely and uneasy transfer student,
that's really cold of you guys!

00:04:32.890 --> 00:04:35.580
Since there's not a whole lot of guys around here, let's get along, okay?

00:04:35.580 --> 00:04:37.320
If this is about baseball, I won't do it.

00:04:37.320 --> 00:04:37.960
What?

00:04:38.430 --> 00:04:39.920
We heard from Fuji...

00:04:39.920 --> 00:04:42.930
You came here to start a baseball team, right?

00:04:43.310 --> 00:04:44.560
Sorry but... nobody here has any interest in playing baseball.

00:04:44.560 --> 00:04:46.640
Sorry but... nobody here has any interest in playing baseball.

00:04:47.970 --> 00:04:48.890
Bye then.

00:04:48.890 --> 00:04:50.470
H-Hey!

00:04:51.850 --> 00:04:52.940
Idiot!

00:04:52.940 --> 00:04:57.150
There's no way that someone who plays baseball would come to Seishuu!

00:05:02.910 --> 00:05:04.830
I heard everything...

00:05:06.450 --> 00:05:09.230
W-Who are you!? Don't startle me like that! 

00:05:09.230 --> 00:05:11.630
A baseball team, huh? Sounds good!

00:05:11.630 --> 00:05:14.340
Two people holding hands and heading towards their dreams...{AMS: "taking" to "holding"}

00:05:14.340 --> 00:05:17.340
it feels like youth! 

00:05:18.250 --> 00:05:20.340
I'm Nakamura Miho.

00:05:20.340 --> 00:05:22.020
I'll be part of your baseball team!

00:05:28.440 --> 00:05:31.200
I don't have any money left over from summer break...

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:33.360
and there's nowhere to go.

00:05:34.310 --> 00:05:36.520
Man, I want to play in a game soon!

00:05:36.520 --> 00:05:39.630
That's right! I want to hit a home run at Koshien!

00:05:39.630 --> 00:05:41.700
Seriously? I want to catch with this glove and... 

00:05:45.840 --> 00:05:50.740
<i>I have no interest in a loser like you who spends all his free time doing nothing.{AMS: 21:39 major 3 - 1}</i>

00:05:51.780 --> 00:05:52.820
Wait a minute.

00:05:53.290 --> 00:05:57.350
This could be my chance to get Kaoru-chan to notice me.

00:05:58.910 --> 00:06:01.080
Hey! Wait a minute!

00:06:01.600 --> 00:06:05.800
Didn't I say I'd join the baseball club and we'd go to Koshien together?

00:06:07.760 --> 00:06:10.680
I'm looking for male members.

00:06:10.680 --> 00:06:13.270
If it was you, you wouldn't be able to participate in games, right?

00:06:13.270 --> 00:06:15.140
Oh... is that so?

00:06:18.190 --> 00:06:20.450
Then, I can be the manager!

00:06:20.870 --> 00:06:24.210
I'll help you recruit members!

00:06:24.210 --> 00:06:25.030
All right?

00:06:26.190 --> 00:06:29.750
I-I didn't ask for your help! What is up with you!? 

00:06:29.750 --> 00:06:31.450
Get off of me...!

00:06:31.450 --> 00:06:32.920
Hey! Shigeno!

00:06:34.260 --> 00:06:35.380
Can I talk to you for a minute?

00:06:35.380 --> 00:06:36.510
{Huh?}

00:06:37.140 --> 00:06:38.380
Fuji...

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:43.760
You're really going to play baseball?

00:06:44.140 --> 00:06:48.370
Yeah, under one condition.

00:06:50.270 --> 00:06:52.550
Let me be the ace and fourth batter.

00:06:53.850 --> 00:06:55.290
What?

00:06:55.290 --> 00:06:57.790
If you can't agree, then it's a no.

00:06:59.710 --> 00:07:01.310
Are you an idiot?

00:07:01.310 --> 00:07:05.540
There's no way that a useless guy like you will be able to play baseball.

00:07:05.540 --> 00:07:08.500
You're annoying, so why don't you disappear?

00:07:08.500 --> 00:07:13.150
H-Hey! He's finally willing to play so don't say unnecessary things!

00:07:13.150 --> 00:07:14.000
What?

00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:20.680
Even if such a guy joins, he won't be of much use.
I'll bring better baseball players from other schools here.

00:07:16.040 --> 00:07:20.680
{I'll bring better baseball players from other schools here.}

00:07:20.680 --> 00:07:23.520
There's no point if players from other schools join!

00:07:23.520 --> 00:07:26.690
Then, let's have a challenge. 

00:07:24.170 --> 00:07:25.090
{Huh?}{AMS: don't need this}

00:07:28.020 --> 00:07:30.820
We'll each hit and pitch ten times.

00:07:30.820 --> 00:07:35.260
The person who gets the most hits off of the other party will be the ace and fourth batter.

00:07:35.260 --> 00:07:36.850
How about that?

00:07:36.850 --> 00:07:43.320
W-Well, it's fine if you win, but what'll you do if I win?

00:07:43.320 --> 00:07:47.850
Didn't I say that if I'm not the ace and fourth batter, I won't play baseball?

00:07:49.430 --> 00:07:51.110
Men don't go back on their word!

00:07:51.510 --> 00:07:53.070
<i>Wait a minute...</i>

00:07:54.990 --> 00:08:00.000
When I was in elementary school,
I was a pitcher on my Little League team.

00:08:00.340 --> 00:08:03.180
If you think you can get a hit off of me so easily, you're hugely mistaken!

00:08:03.690 --> 00:08:05.580
<i>L-Little League?</i>

00:08:06.040 --> 00:08:10.370
<i>Hasn't he heard that I went to Kaido?</i>

00:08:10.370 --> 00:08:12.060
Here I go!

00:08:17.210 --> 00:08:18.490
{Eh? Huh? Hahahaha!}

00:08:18.490 --> 00:08:19.070
{Eh? Huh? Hahahaha!}

00:08:20.210 --> 00:08:23.730
That didn't count. My shoulder wasn't warmed up yet!

00:08:31.370 --> 00:08:33.240
Damn it!

00:08:43.290 --> 00:08:45.830
T-That's strange.

00:08:47.480 --> 00:08:48.620
How pathetic.

00:08:49.220 --> 00:08:51.530
Do you... want to hit first?

00:08:52.970 --> 00:08:55.310
{Eh? }Y-Yeah, t-that's right...{stuttering at "that" added by sangofe}

00:08:57.820 --> 00:09:00.060
Well, if I had to pick one,

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:02.770
I'm definitely better at batting!

00:09:03.220 --> 00:09:06.100
I was always the fourth batter on my Little League team.

00:09:06.100 --> 00:09:08.390
<i>I was thinking about faking a strike,</i>

00:09:08.390 --> 00:09:10.230
<i>but he can't even pitch a strike!</i>

00:09:10.770 --> 00:09:12.690
All right! Bring it on!

00:09:14.300 --> 00:09:17.800
<i>Well, forget it. I'll just pitch lightly and let him hit it so he'll feel good about himself.</i>

00:09:17.800 --> 00:09:20.030
<i>It'll be good if he simply joins the baseball team. </i>

00:09:26.330 --> 00:09:28.520
What's wrong? That was a strike.

00:09:28.520 --> 00:09:29.500
I know!

00:09:30.210 --> 00:09:33.170
<i>This guy... his pitches are pretty fast!</i>

00:09:39.690 --> 00:09:40.900
What?

00:09:41.620 --> 00:09:44.680
<i>What is he doing? I'm only pitching at about 100km/h.</i>

00:09:46.820 --> 00:09:50.750
Boon, boon, boon... it's not a bee's song, you know? {Note: *Boon* = sound of the swing of the bat & the sound of bees}

00:09:51.430 --> 00:09:53.040
Shut up!

00:09:59.180 --> 00:10:00.160
Could it be!? 

00:10:06.190 --> 00:10:10.090
<i>No way... They're all hitting the block in the middle!</i>

00:10:10.090 --> 00:10:12.130
Damn!

00:10:13.050 --> 00:10:14.360
This is the last one.

00:10:16.180 --> 00:10:18.390
<i>Why can't I hit them!?</i>

00:10:28.760 --> 00:10:29.780
How pathetic.

00:10:30.160 --> 00:10:33.430
I guess you're really just a guy who's all talk.

00:10:37.400 --> 00:10:40.020
Hey, don't worry about it! I get it! I get it!

00:10:40.020 --> 00:10:41.920
You can be the ace and fourth batter. 

00:10:41.920 --> 00:10:43.190
So you'll join the baseball team, right?

00:10:43.190 --> 00:10:44.830
Don't take me for an idiot!

00:10:44.830 --> 00:10:47.260
Why would I ever want to play baseball again!?

00:10:53.240 --> 00:10:55.460
And... one guy disappears.

00:10:57.080 --> 00:10:59.210
Dinner's ready!

00:11:02.970 --> 00:11:04.640
How's it going... Goro?

00:11:05.200 --> 00:11:08.010
Are you having any success in recruiting baseball members?

00:11:09.050 --> 00:11:12.940
It seems like no one wants... to play baseball.

00:11:12.940 --> 00:11:16.190
Well, I never thought that it'd be easy to begin with.

00:11:16.870 --> 00:11:20.440
Is that so? Well, take your time and don't get impatient.

00:11:20.440 --> 00:11:23.980
You tend to overdo it when it comes to baseball.

00:11:26.270 --> 00:11:27.660
You too, Dad.

00:11:28.110 --> 00:11:30.670
You're getting old, so don't overdo it.

00:11:31.260 --> 00:11:35.280
I want to go into the next game in the best shape possible.

00:11:35.280 --> 00:11:38.050
I won't lose to you just yet!

00:11:39.260 --> 00:11:42.010
How could I lose to an old man?

00:11:45.010 --> 00:11:45.890
How's this!? {added by sangofe}

00:11:45.890 --> 00:11:47.280
It's time for dinner.

00:11:51.440 --> 00:11:54.810
I said it's time for dinner! Knock it off already, you two!

00:11:54.810 --> 00:11:56.580
Y-Yes!

00:11:57.900 --> 00:12:02.900
This is a free fansub.

00:11:57.900 --> 00:12:02.900
Not for sale or rent.

00:12:03.910 --> 00:12:04.860
Huh?

00:12:06.110 --> 00:12:07.750
Well... like I said...

00:12:07.750 --> 00:12:10.680
I was wondering if you were interested in baseball.

00:12:10.680 --> 00:12:14.530
If you're not in any clubs, it's fine, right? Baseball's really fun.

00:12:17.380 --> 00:12:19.020
Sorry,

00:12:19.020 --> 00:12:22.600
we're not really interested in sports related clubs, so please ask someone else.

00:12:22.600 --> 00:12:26.260
W-Wait a second!
I'm asking you <i>because</i> there's no one else!

00:12:26.700 --> 00:12:28.240
P-Please stop it! 

00:12:28.240 --> 00:12:29.900
The transfer student's being violent!

00:12:29.900 --> 00:12:30.940
How am I being violent!?

00:12:31.890 --> 00:12:35.160
How can this be? All seven of them said no.

00:12:35.160 --> 00:12:40.360
I didn't know that there were so many guys in this world with no interest in baseball.

00:12:40.360 --> 00:12:41.750
Well, of course.

00:12:42.250 --> 00:12:47.910
If they seriously wanted to play sports, they wouldn't have come to Seishuu, where there isn't a lot of guys.

00:12:47.910 --> 00:12:51.910
Besides, guys who don't like sports clubs won't want to practice.

00:12:51.910 --> 00:12:54.260
"It's too hot. It's too tough. You reek of sweat."

00:12:54.760 --> 00:12:59.250
Even if you had invited them properly, there's no way the guys here would want to play baseball.

00:13:00.120 --> 00:13:02.350
<i>Properly invite them, huh?</i>

00:13:06.380 --> 00:13:08.260
{Huh?}Being members in name only is fine?

00:13:08.700 --> 00:13:12.970
Yeah, you guys won't have to practice at all.

00:13:12.970 --> 00:13:15.920
You'll belong to the baseball team only in name for the time being,

00:13:15.920 --> 00:13:20.110
and just simply show up during the official games next summer wearing our uniform.

00:13:20.110 --> 00:13:20.990
That's all you have to do.

00:13:20.990 --> 00:13:23.710
See? Sounds easy, right?

00:13:25.730 --> 00:13:28.180
Of course, I'll buy you food on game day.

00:13:28.180 --> 00:13:29.630
I refuse.

00:13:30.080 --> 00:13:33.350
Why do we have to do something like that?

00:13:33.350 --> 00:13:36.100
We'll just lose really badly and be humiliated, right?

00:13:36.100 --> 00:13:39.090
Well, if it's about that, then there's nothing to worry about.

00:13:39.550 --> 00:13:43.930
If I hit home runs and get 27 strikeouts, the game will be over.

00:13:44.350 --> 00:13:49.490
Even during prefectural games, or at Koshien,
 all you have to do is just stand there.

00:13:53.140 --> 00:13:55.150
What the hell are you saying?

00:13:55.150 --> 00:13:59.870
Even we know the level of high school baseball in Kanagawa.

00:14:01.560 --> 00:14:02.660
Laughing, huh?

00:14:02.660 --> 00:14:06.660
Then if I can prove it to you,
you'll join the baseball team, right?

00:14:07.230 --> 00:14:09.780
Y-Yeah, that is...

00:14:09.780 --> 00:14:11.620
if you prove it.

00:14:11.620 --> 00:14:14.270
All right, it's a promise then!

00:14:16.230 --> 00:14:18.970
H-Hey! What was up with that promise back there?

00:14:19.350 --> 00:14:22.810
Don't tell me you're serious about going to Koshien with a team from this school?

00:14:22.810 --> 00:14:25.290
Huh? Of course I'm being serious.

00:14:25.290 --> 00:14:27.890
That's the reason why I came to Seishuu.

00:14:28.440 --> 00:14:29.460
Seishuu!

00:14:29.460 --> 00:14:31.110
<i>So cool!</i>

00:14:29.670 --> 00:14:30.150
Fight on! Fight on! Fight on!

00:14:30.150 --> 00:14:30.520
Fight on! Fight on! Fight on!

00:14:30.520 --> 00:14:30.910
Fight on! Fight on! Fight on!

00:14:30.910 --> 00:14:31.270
Fight on! Fight on! Fight on!

00:14:31.270 --> 00:14:31.650
Fight on! Fight on! Fight on!

00:14:31.650 --> 00:14:32.400
Fight on! Fight on! Fight on!

00:14:32.400 --> 00:14:33.780
Seishuu!

00:14:33.780 --> 00:14:34.280
Fight on! Fight on! Fight on!

00:14:34.280 --> 00:14:34.610
Fight on! Fight on! Fight on!

00:14:34.610 --> 00:14:34.980
Fight on! Fight on! Fight on!

00:14:34.980 --> 00:14:35.360
Fight on! Fight on! Fight on!

00:14:35.360 --> 00:14:35.770
Fight on! Fight on! Fight on!

00:14:35.770 --> 00:14:36.240
Fight on! Fight on! Fight on!

00:14:36.710 --> 00:14:38.890
Yo, Shimizu! Working hard, huh?

00:14:40.290 --> 00:14:41.680
Sorry. Go on ahead of me.

00:14:42.510 --> 00:14:43.980
Seishuu!

00:14:43.980 --> 00:14:44.480
Fight on! Fight on! Fight on!

00:14:44.480 --> 00:14:44.860
Fight on! Fight on! Fight on!

00:14:44.710 --> 00:14:47.010
So, how's it going with gathering teammates?

00:14:44.860 --> 00:14:45.220
Fight on! Fight on! Fight on!

00:14:45.220 --> 00:14:45.620
Fight on! Fight on! Fight on!

00:14:45.620 --> 00:14:45.950
Fight on! Fight on! Fight on!

00:14:45.950 --> 00:14:46.540
Fight on! Fight on! Fight on!

00:14:46.540 --> 00:14:47.960
Seishuu!

00:14:47.010 --> 00:14:48.960
Well, you see,

00:14:49.350 --> 00:14:51.950
no one wants to join.

00:14:51.950 --> 00:14:55.370
I have a favor to ask of you.

00:14:55.370 --> 00:14:57.760
And... who is that girl?

00:14:58.620 --> 00:15:00.410
Well, I don't really know. She just all of a sudden-

00:15:00.410 --> 00:15:01.630
Well!

00:15:01.630 --> 00:15:05.090
I'm the baseball manager, Nakamura Miho!

00:15:05.610 --> 00:15:07.550
And you, too. What are you to Goro?

00:15:07.550 --> 00:15:11.330
W-What am I? Just his childhood friend.

00:15:11.330 --> 00:15:15.500
Oh really? I'm relieved to hear that you're just his childhood friend.

00:15:15.500 --> 00:15:19.540
So, you're perfectly fine with me being darling's manager, correct?

00:15:19.540 --> 00:15:20.870
Darling?

00:15:21.680 --> 00:15:26.080
I see. I always thought it was a little
 strange for you to come to Seishuu,

00:15:26.480 --> 00:15:31.030
but in the end, you transferred here so you could do stuff like this, right?

00:15:31.030 --> 00:15:31.530
{Eh?}

00:15:31.440 --> 00:15:33.190
I wish you two happiness!

00:15:33.190 --> 00:15:35.290
It's not! Hey! Shimizu!

00:15:35.290 --> 00:15:36.510
Hey!

00:15:37.120 --> 00:15:38.450
Why don't you leave her alone?

00:15:38.450 --> 00:15:40.290
How long are you going to keep holding onto me for!? 

00:15:42.790 --> 00:15:46.270
I didn't think he'd become so frivolous.

00:15:46.270 --> 00:15:48.040
If this is the case, isn't he just like Fuji?

00:15:53.670 --> 00:15:54.810
<i>Fuji?</i>

00:15:58.690 --> 00:16:01.270
Damn! I'm not done yet!

00:16:03.670 --> 00:16:06.490
Shouldn't you bring your elbows in a bit?

00:16:08.220 --> 00:16:09.940
K-Kaoru-chan!

00:16:13.300 --> 00:16:14.900
Are you all right?

00:16:15.360 --> 00:16:17.360
Yeah. I'm fine.

00:16:17.980 --> 00:16:21.500
You actually come to places like this? I'm a little surprised.

00:16:22.760 --> 00:16:26.660
Your childhood friend... It's Shigeno, right?

00:16:27.430 --> 00:16:31.080
Yesterday, he beat me pretty badly at baseball.

00:16:31.910 --> 00:16:34.850
I couldn't even touch the ball once.

00:16:35.760 --> 00:16:38.810
That's the first time that I've felt so disappointed in my life.

00:16:39.220 --> 00:16:44.020
I just felt like I had to try one more time to get revenge.

00:16:45.660 --> 00:16:48.180
Well then, I guess I'll hit another round.

00:16:48.180 --> 00:16:50.520
Don't watch too much, because I look really uncool.

00:16:50.520 --> 00:16:51.650
You don't look uncool!

00:16:53.270 --> 00:16:55.320
You don't look uncool at all.

00:16:57.080 --> 00:17:01.320
If you're okay with me, how about I help you with that revenge of yours?

00:17:04.830 --> 00:17:06.910
What did I do?

00:17:07.460 --> 00:17:10.240
You're not with your lover today, huh?

00:17:10.240 --> 00:17:11.880
Who's my lover!?

00:17:11.880 --> 00:17:15.920
That woman is just pretending to be the manager!

00:17:15.920 --> 00:17:19.580
Even so, you two seemed awfully close to each other.

00:17:20.480 --> 00:17:21.260
Besides that...

00:17:21.970 --> 00:17:24.110
I have a favor to ask of you.

00:17:25.720 --> 00:17:28.760
I'm fine with playing catcher,

00:17:28.760 --> 00:17:31.790
but are you serious about winning a game by yourself?

00:17:31.790 --> 00:17:32.840
Yeah.

00:17:34.390 --> 00:17:36.550
All right. I guess we should start with crouching now.

00:17:36.550 --> 00:17:37.710
Y-Yeah.

00:17:38.880 --> 00:17:41.390
Throw it softly at first, okay? Softly.

00:17:41.390 --> 00:17:45.420
Even though I play softball,
I haven't caught a baseball in a while.

00:17:45.420 --> 00:17:47.670
Yeah, I know.

00:17:48.180 --> 00:17:49.270
Here I go!

00:17:55.200 --> 00:17:57.860
As expected, Shimizu! It's easy for you!

00:17:57.860 --> 00:17:59.390
<i>It hurts!</i>

00:17:59.840 --> 00:18:02.980
<i>That idiot! Even though I said "softly"!</i>

00:18:02.980 --> 00:18:06.100
<i>If I don't concentrate on catching, I'll seriously get hurt.</i>

00:18:14.810 --> 00:18:18.660
Okay! All right then, I'm going to start getting serious.

00:18:19.400 --> 00:18:21.070
<i>N-No way!</i>

00:18:21.070 --> 00:18:23.130
<i>Up until now he was seriously throwing lightly?</i>

00:18:26.260 --> 00:18:27.290
W-Wait!

00:18:39.340 --> 00:18:40.970
{Huh? }What're you doing?

00:18:41.400 --> 00:18:43.680
W-What's up with that pitch?

00:18:43.680 --> 00:18:45.150
{What?}

00:18:45.950 --> 00:18:48.670
Don't tell me... you can't catch it?

00:18:48.670 --> 00:18:50.990
There's no way I can catch that kind of pitch!

00:18:50.990 --> 00:18:52.950
W-What!?

00:18:53.250 --> 00:18:57.860
That's right. At first, Kaido's catchers had a hard time too.

00:18:57.870 --> 00:19:00.060
I guess it would be impossible for me to expect Shimizu to catch it.

00:18:58.990 --> 00:19:00.080
<i>This guy...</i>

00:19:00.650 --> 00:19:03.790
<i>he got even better and came back.</i>

00:19:04.170 --> 00:19:06.910
Hey! So you're here, huh?

00:19:07.490 --> 00:19:08.330
Fuji?

00:19:08.710 --> 00:19:14.210
Kaoru-chan, let me show you the results of the special training I did after you gave me some advice.

00:19:15.340 --> 00:19:16.970
I challenge you, Shigeno!

00:19:16.970 --> 00:19:19.630
I'm not the same guy I was last time!

00:19:20.390 --> 00:19:21.310
Wait a minute!

00:19:21.720 --> 00:19:26.640
I did give you some advice but from just a day's worth of training there's no way you can get revenge on him.

00:19:29.850 --> 00:19:34.520
What is it? Are you saying we should have another "swinging at air and haphazard pitching" challenge?

00:19:37.830 --> 00:19:40.150
I told you that I'm different from before!

00:19:40.590 --> 00:19:41.970
I will beat you... and regain my pride as a man!

00:19:41.970 --> 00:19:44.420
I will beat you... and regain my pride as a man!

00:19:44.420 --> 00:19:46.330
But if I lose...

00:19:46.580 --> 00:19:48.330
I'll become a member of the baseball team!

00:19:53.830 --> 00:19:57.430
Just like last time, it'll be a battle with ten pitches. Fine with you?

00:19:57.430 --> 00:20:00.640
Yeah, I got it, I got it. Hurry up and pitch.

00:20:01.240 --> 00:20:04.390
I'm different from who I was before!

00:20:09.190 --> 00:20:11.560
Indeed, your control has gotten better.

00:20:12.560 --> 00:20:14.490
D-Damn!

00:20:24.490 --> 00:20:27.520
What's wrong? Is it okay if we call it my win now?

00:20:28.320 --> 00:20:31.030
Shut up! The battle starts now!

00:20:31.880 --> 00:20:36.670
<i>It's impossible, Fuji. There's too much of a difference in your abilites.{The level of your skills are too different.}</i>

00:20:38.240 --> 00:20:39.340
Damn it!

00:20:40.650 --> 00:20:42.260
Oh, not good!

00:20:50.870 --> 00:20:52.800
{Huh? }Well, we'll count that one as an out.

00:20:52.800 --> 00:20:55.770
With this, I hit nine out of ten, right?

00:21:04.470 --> 00:21:05.070
Here I go.

00:21:05.070 --> 00:21:08.070
<i>All I have to do is hit ten out of ten!</i>

00:21:22.870 --> 00:21:26.190
<i>What the hell is this? It's totally different from the last time!</i>

00:21:26.190 --> 00:21:29.400
All right. The end. I win.

00:21:29.400 --> 00:21:31.840
W-Wait! It's not over yet!

00:21:31.840 --> 00:21:33.280
I'm telling you it's over.

00:21:33.280 --> 00:21:36.810
You won't be able to even touch my pitches!{AMS: "the balls I pitch" to "my pitches"}

00:21:41.540 --> 00:21:43.520
Why don't you pitch for him, Honda?

00:21:45.510 --> 00:21:47.980
Why not? Just throw him ten pitches.

00:21:48.940 --> 00:21:50.770
Kaoru-chan...

00:22:05.630 --> 00:22:08.310
<i>I've never seen pitches this fast!</i>

00:22:13.900 --> 00:22:14.860
This is the last one.

00:22:31.380 --> 00:22:33.210
I-I did it!

00:22:34.090 --> 00:22:37.170
I did it! I hit it!

00:22:37.600 --> 00:22:39.120
Did you see that?

00:22:40.630 --> 00:22:41.870
Fuji...

00:22:43.750 --> 00:22:45.540
Play baseball!

00:22:48.340 --> 00:22:49.550
Yeah...

00:22:50.920 --> 00:22:52.770
Because it <i>was</i> a promise after all...

00:22:53.600 --> 00:22:55.470
I'll join the baseball team!

00:22:59.170 --> 00:23:01.400
That last one, you put less strength into it, right?

00:23:05.760 --> 00:23:06.980
Who knows?

00:24:41.420 --> 00:24:44.680
In trying to start up a baseball team, the problem is Yamazumi.{AMS: "Going towards starting the baseball team" to "In trying to start up a baseball team"}

00:24:44.680 --> 00:24:47.940
Just then, there are big problems at home.

00:24:47.940 --> 00:24:49.410
Mom's leaving the house?

00:24:49.410 --> 00:24:51.510
What exactly is the matter, Dad?

00:24:52.760 --> 00:24:53.520
Next time, on Major:

00:24:54.120 --> 00:24:55.310
Father to Son!

00:24:55.310 --> 00:24:57.670
Run to the stage of your dreams!
